IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (Exemption) (Amendment) Order 2014 (S 600/2014), made under s 60 of the Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-exemption-amendment-order-2014/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-S600-2014.txt (e-Gazette PDF, pdftotext -layout, unedited). Quotations below are lines of THAT file; `srcrefs.py` is run on this module against it.
-- First published 15 September 2014 at 5.00 pm; "shall come into operation on 15 September 2014" (paragraph 1).
-- It amends the Broadcasting (Exemption) Order (O 1). The Order as the Revised Edition 2004 prints it is in `sgba-i-or1-2004.l4`; the text after this Order is `sgba-i-exempt-1996.l4` (lawplain).

§ `Paragraphs 1 to 3`

-- src:3 | First published in the Government Gazette, Electronic Edition, on 15th September 2014 at 5.00 pm.
-- src:20 | 1. This Order may be cited as the Broadcasting (Exemption)
-- src:21 | (Amendment) Order 2014 and shall come into operation on
-- src:22 | 15 September 2014.
@ref S 600/2014 publication line and para 1 (commencement) (src:3-22)
GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 600/2014 the amendments are in operation on` MEANS
    `the day of the conduct` AT LEAST (Date 15 9 2014)

-- src:25 | 2. Paragraph 1 of the Broadcasting (Exemption) Order (O 1) is
-- src:26 | amended by inserting, immediately after the words “Notification
-- src:27 | (N 1)” in sub-paragraph (f), the words “or subject to a notice under
-- src:28 | paragraph 3A(1) of that Notification”.
@ref S 600/2014 para 2: O 1 para 1(f) amended ("or subject to a notice under paragraph 3A(1) of that Notification") (src:25-28)
GIVEN `it is a computer on-line service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is subject to a class licence under the Broadcasting (Class Licence) Notification (N 1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is subject to a notice under paragraph 3A(1) of that Notification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 600/2014 O 1 para 1(f) the service is exempt from sections 8 and 9 (as amended)` MEANS
    `it is a computer on-line service` AND (NOT `it is subject to a class licence under the Broadcasting (Class Licence) Notification (N 1)`) AND (NOT `it is subject to a notice under paragraph 3A(1) of that Notification`)

-- src:31 | 3. Paragraph 2 of the Broadcasting (Exemption) Order is deleted.
@ref S 600/2014 para 3: O 1 para 2 deleted (src:31)
GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 600/2014 O 1 para 2 (the exemption includes computer on-line services of individual Internet Content Providers) still has effect on` MEANS
    `the day of the conduct` LESS THAN (Date 15 9 2014)
